msgid "充分利用核数"
msgstr "Fully utilize the cores"

msgid "昇腾NPU具备多个计算核心，合理分配并充分利用所有可用核心，是提升算子性能的关键因素之一。 在调用Triton内核函数时，通过设置launch参数控制使用的核数量。以GELU算子为例："
msgstr "The Ascend NPU has multiple compute cores. Properly allocating and fully utilizing all available cores is one of the key factors for improving operator performance. When calling a Triton kernel, control the number of cores used by setting the launch parameter. Using the GELU operator as an example:"

msgid ""
"triton_gelu[n, 1, 1](...)  # 第一个参数表示使用的核数，n表示使用n个核\n"
msgstr ""
"triton_gelu[n, 1, 1](...)  # The first parameter indicates the number of cores used; n indicates that n cores are used\n"

msgid "通过对核数的调优，可实现对所有计算资源的充分调度和利用，从而最大化并行度与吞吐量。未启用 `auto-blockify`（见下节）时，启动grid的核数需小于等于AI Core总数（同时grid各维度大小受65,535上限约束）。"
msgstr "By tuning the number of cores, you can fully schedule and utilize all computing resources, thereby maximizing parallelism and throughput. When `auto-blockify` is not enabled (see the next section), the number of cores launched by the grid must be less than or equal to the total number of AI Cores (the size of each grid dimension is also constrained by an upper limit of 65,535)."

msgid "auto-blockify：突破65,535逻辑块上限"
msgstr "auto-blockify: Breaking the 65,535 logical block limit"

msgid "社区Triton在NVIDIA GPU上把grid视为纯逻辑维度 —— `n` 个逻辑块按1:1映射到 `n` 个硬件块，运行时由硬件分发到各SM，每个块不需要内部循环。昇腾上由于[多核任务并行策略](#多核任务并行策略)中描述的物理核强绑定，可启动的grid上限被限制在65,535，对含百万级逻辑工作项的kernel（autotune后的reduce/scan、megablocks风格的稀疏kernel等）过于严苛。"
msgstr "Community Triton treats the grid as a purely logical dimension on NVIDIA GPUs — `n` logical blocks map 1:1 to `n` hardware blocks, and the hardware dispatches them to each SM at runtime. Each block does not require internal loops. On Ascend, due to the strict physical core binding described in [Multi-core Task Parallel Strategy](#多核任务并行策略), the maximum number of launchable grids is limited to 65,535, which is too restrictive for kernels containing millions of logical work items (reduce/scan after autotune, megablocks-style sparse kernels, and so on)."

msgid "`auto-blockify`（`SIMTAutoBlockify` 编译期pass + 配套的运行期cap）通过\"编译期视为逻辑、启动期折叠到物理核\"消除该限制："
msgstr "`auto-blockify` (`SIMTAutoBlockify` compile-time pass + the accompanying runtime cap) eliminates this limitation by \"treating as logical at compile time and folding to physical cores at launch time\":"

msgid "**编译期**：Triton pass把kernel函数体包进一层 `scf.for`，迭代变量由 `gpu.linear_block_id` 提供。chunk大小 = `ceildiv(logical_block_count, physical_core_count)`，每个物理块依次跑 `chunk` 个逻辑block id。"
msgstr "**Compile time**: The Triton pass wraps the kernel function body in an `scf.for` loop, with the iteration variable provided by `gpu.linear_block_id`. The chunk size = `ceildiv(logical_block_count, physical_core_count)`, and each physical block sequentially runs `chunk` logical block ids."

msgid "**运行期**：传给launcher的block-count参数从逻辑grid clamp到 `physical_core_count`，与编译期的折叠保持一致。"
msgstr "**Runtime**: The block-count parameter passed to the launcher is clamped from the logical grid to `physical_core_count`, consistent with the compile-time folding."

msgid "编译期和运行期共享同一份后端内部策略。自动block mapping由后端统一启用，编译器生成的IR安全标记会排除不适用的kernel。因此，编译期循环包与运行期cap始终同步，不存在kernel按一种模式编译却按另一种模式启动的情形。"
msgstr "Compile time and runtime share the same internal backend policy. The backend uniformly enables automatic block mapping, and the IR safety markers generated by the compiler exclude inapplicable kernels. Therefore, the compile-time loop package and the runtime cap remain synchronized. There is no case where a kernel is compiled in one mode but launched in another mode."

msgid "从GPU Triton kernel移植时的注意事项："
msgstr "Precautions when porting from a GPU Triton kernel:"

msgid "grid大于65,535可直接运行，无需手动把外层维度折叠进kernel函数体。"
msgstr "You can directly run a grid larger than 65,535 without manually folding the outer dimension into the kernel function body."

msgid "逻辑块之间必须保持顺序无关（循环按chunk顺序访问）。依赖严格逻辑块id顺序的kernel（如基于特定顺序的跨块同步）需要改写。"
msgstr "Logical blocks must remain order-independent (loops access chunks in chunk order). Kernels that depend on a strict logical block ID order (such as cross-block synchronization based on a specific order) need to be rewritten."

msgid "per-block workspace分配从 `O(logical_block_count)` 降到 `O(physical_core_count)`，因为workspace在内层 `scf.for` 各次迭代间复用。"
msgstr "The per-block workspace allocation decreases from `O(logical_block_count)` to `O(physical_core_count)` because the workspace is reused across iterations of the inner `scf.for`."

msgid "单核数据搬运策略"
msgstr "Single-Core Data Movement Strategy"

msgid "数据切分Tiling"
msgstr "Data Tiling"

msgid "写Triton内核函数时，合理的数据切分策略对性能优化至关重要。通过调整不同的切分粒度参数，可以在不同维度上平衡计算负载与内存访问效率。"
msgstr "When you write Triton kernel functions, a proper data tiling strategy is crucial for performance optimization. By adjusting different tiling granularity parameters, you can balance the computational load and memory access efficiency across different dimensions."

msgid "常见的切分参数包括："
msgstr "Common tiling parameters include:"

msgid ""
"ncore：使用的核数（跨核切分）\n"
"xblock：核间数据块大小（核间切分）\n"
"xblock_sub：核内切分粒度（核内细粒度划分）\n"
msgstr ""
"ncore: Number of cores used (cross-core tiling)\n"
"xblock: Inter-core data block size (inter-core tiling)\n"
"xblock_sub: Intra-core tiling granularity (fine-grained intra-core partitioning)\n"

msgid "开发者可根据实际场景手动选择最优的切分配置，使得每次计算尽可能充分利用片上内存（On-chip Memory），避免频繁访问全局内存（Global Memory）造成的 性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "You can manually select the optimal tiling configuration based on your scenario. This maximizes on-chip memory usage for each computation, avoiding performance bottlenecks caused by frequent global memory access."

msgid "以GELU算子为例，通过调整切分参数，可以有效适配片上内存容量限制，从而提升执行效率。"
msgstr "Using the GELU operator as an example, adjusting the tiling parameters effectively accommodates on-chip memory capacity limits, thereby improving execution efficiency."

msgid "注：Atlas 800T A2训练服务器、Atlas 800I A2推理服务器的片上内存容量为192KB，因此在设计切分策略时需考虑该限制，确保每轮计算的数据量不超过片上内存容量。"
msgstr "Note: The on-chip memory capacity of the Atlas 800T A2 training server and Atlas 800I A2 inference server is 192 KB. Therefore, consider this limit when designing the tiling strategy to ensure that the data volume per computation round does not exceed the on-chip memory capacity."

msgid "GELU算子示例"
msgstr "GELU operator example"

msgid "GELU算子开发示例，使用3种方式计算结果。"
msgstr "The GELU operator development sample uses three methods to calculate the result."

msgid "`standard_unary`为标准Torch计算；`triton_easy_kernel`为简单Triton实现；`triton_better_kernel`为更高效的Triton实现。"
msgstr "`standard_unary` is a standard Torch computation; `triton_easy_kernel` is a simple Triton implementation; `triton_better_kernel` is a more efficient Triton implementation."

msgid "标准Torch写法"
msgstr "Standard Torch syntax"

msgid "输入tensor x0，经过torch计算实现GELU算子，返回结果值。"
msgstr "Input tensor x0, implement the GELU operator using torch computation, and return the result value."

msgid ""
"def standard_unary(x0):\n"
"    res = x0 * 0.5 * (1.0 + torch.erf(x0 / torch.sqrt(torch.tensor(2.0))))\n"
"    return res\n"
msgstr ""
"def standard_unary(x0):\n"
"    res = x0 * 0.5 * (1.0 + torch.erf(x0 / torch.sqrt(torch.tensor(2.0))))\n"
"    return res\n"

msgid "简单Triton写法"
msgstr "Simple Triton Syntax"

msgid "以下是一个使用Triton编写的简单内核示例，用于展示如何定义和调用一个基本的Triton内核函数。此示例实现了一个简单的数学运算（GELU激活函数）。"
msgstr "The following is a simple kernel sample written in Triton to show how to define and call a basic Triton kernel function. This sample implements a simple mathematical operation (GELU activation function)."

msgid ""
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# 定义triton_kernel核函数\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_easy_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, NUMEL: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    idx_block = tl.arange(0, NUMEL)\n"
"    x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + idx_block)\n"
"    ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"    tl.store(out_ptr0 + idx_block, ret)\n"
"\n"
"# 调用triton_kernel核函数\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"triton_easy_kernel[1, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel())\n"
msgstr ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# Define the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_easy_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, NUMEL: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    idx_block = tl.arange(0, NUMEL)\n"
"    x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + idx_block)\n"
"    ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"    tl.store(out_ptr0 + idx_block, ret)\n"
"\n"
"# Call the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(32768, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"triton_easy_kernel[1, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel())\n"

msgid "注意事项"
msgstr "Precautions"

msgid "内存限制：上述写法中，所有输入数据一次性被加载到内存中进行计算。如果输入张量过大，可能会超出单个内核的片上内存容量，导致内存溢出错误。 因此，这种简单的写法更适合于小规模张量的计算或用于理解Triton内核的基本写法和调用方式。"
msgstr "Memory limit: In the preceding approach, all input data is loaded into memory at once for computation. If the input tensor is too large, it may exceed the on-chip memory capacity of a single kernel, causing an out-of-memory error. Therefore, this simple approach is more suitable for small-scale tensor computation or for understanding the basic implementation and invocation methods of Triton kernels."

msgid "适用场景：尽管这种方法有助于快速理解和入门Triton编程，但对于大规模数据集或高性能要求的应用场景，建议采用更复杂的数据切分策略（如Tiling）， 以充分利用硬件资源并避免内存溢出问题。通过这种方式，开发者可以快速上手Triton编程，同时了解如何定义、调用以及优化Triton内核函数。"
msgstr "Applicable scenario: Although this method helps you quickly understand and get started with Triton programming, for large-scale datasets or high-performance scenarios, we recommend a more complex data splitting strategy (such as tiling). This fully utilizes hardware resources and avoids memory overflow issues. Through this method, you can quickly get started with Triton programming and learn how to define, call, and optimize Triton kernels."

msgid "更高效Triton写法"
msgstr "More efficient Triton writing practices"

msgid "在昇腾NPU上使用Triton编写高性能算子时，为了充分利用硬件资源、避免内存溢出并提升执行效率，通常需要采用数据切分（Tiling）策略。 下面是一个经过优化的Triton内核实现示例，适用于大规模张量计算。"
msgstr "When you write high-performance operators using Triton on the Ascend NPU, adopt a data tiling strategy. This helps fully utilize hardware resources, avoid memory overflow, and improve execution efficiency. The following is an optimized Triton kernel implementation sample, suitable for large-scale tensor computation."

msgid ""
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# 定义triton_kernel核函数\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_better_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, xnumel, XBLOCK: tl.constexpr, XBLOCK_SUB: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"    for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"        x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"        xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"        x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + x_index, xmask)\n"
"        ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"        tl.store(out_ptr0 + x_index, ret, xmask)\n"
"\n"
"ncore = 32\n"
"xblock = 32768\n"
"xblock_sub = 8192\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(ncore * xblock, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"# 调用triton_kernel核函数\n"
"triton_better_kernel[ncore, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel(), xblock, xblock_sub)\n"
msgstr ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"# Define the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def triton_better_kernel(in_ptr0, out_ptr0, xnumel, XBLOCK: tl.constexpr, XBLOCK_SUB: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"    for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"        x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"        xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"        x = tl.load(in_ptr0 + x_index, xmask)\n"
"        ret = x * 0.5 * (1.0 + tl.erf(x / tl.sqrt(2.0)))\n"
"        tl.store(out_ptr0 + x_index, ret, xmask)\n"
"\n"
"ncore = 32\n"
"xblock = 32768\n"
"xblock_sub = 8192\n"
"x0 = torch.rand(ncore * xblock, device='npu')\n"
"out1 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"# Call the triton_kernel kernel\n"
"triton_better_kernel[ncore, 1, 1](x0, out1, x0.numel(), xblock, xblock_sub)\n"

msgid "关键代码解释："
msgstr "Key code explanation:"

msgid ""
"# 计算当前核处理数据块的起始偏移地址，实现核间切分。每个核仅负责XBLOCK大小的数据范围。\n"
"xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"\n"
"# 在单个核内部进一步细分数据块，每次处理XBLOCK_SUB大小的数据，实现核内切分。\n"
"for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"\n"
"# 构造当前迭代的数据索引数组，用于访问输入和输出张量。\n"
"x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"\n"
"# 设置掩码以防止越界访问，确保只处理合法范围内的数据。\n"
"xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"\n"
"# 分别用于从全局内存加载数据到片上内存，以及将计算结果写回全局内存。\n"
"tl.load() 和tl.store()\n"
msgstr ""
"# Calculate the starting offset address of the data block that the current core processes to implement inter-core splitting. Each core is only responsible for a data range of the XBLOCK size.\n"
"xoffset = tl.program_id(0) * XBLOCK\n"
"\n"
"# Further divide the data block within a single core. Each iteration processes data of the XBLOCK_SUB size to implement intra-core splitting.\n"
"for xoffset_sub in range(0, XBLOCK, XBLOCK_SUB):\n"
"\n"
"# Construct the data index array for the current iteration to access the input and output tensors.\n"
"x_index = xoffset + xoffset_sub + tl.arange(0, XBLOCK_SUB)[:]\n"
"\n"
"# Set a mask to prevent out-of-bounds access and ensure that only data within the valid range is processed.\n"
"xmask = x_index < xnumel\n"
"\n"
"# These functions load data from the global memory to the on-chip memory and write the computation results back to the global memory, respectively.\n"
"tl.load() and tl.store()\n"

